def sum_nonnegative(values: list[int]) -> int:
    return sum(value for value in values if value >= 0)
```

The generator supplies one value at a time. It visits all n inputs, so time is O(n), with O(1) additional space for bounded integers. A normal loop with an accumulator also meets this goal and is equally valid. A list comprehension inside sum() first materializes the matching values, using O(n) additional space. Shorter code is not automatically faster: compare the measurements and prefer clarity. Input storage is excluded from this exercise's allocation measurement.

